WEBVTT

00:00:00.617 --> 00:00:04.589
Welcome to Manage Holdings in Portfolio Tracker This is where

00:00:04.602 --> 00:00:10.005
an account’s positions dividend settings income estimates and transaction history

00:00:10.018 --> 00:00:14.315
come together In this detailed walkthrough we will explain every

00:00:14.328 --> 00:00:18.677
summary box work across the complete holdings table and show

00:00:18.677 --> 00:00:21.451
how the different editing controls are used You will see

00:00:21.451 --> 00:00:25.500
how to add a position correct its information maintain purchase

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:30.083
and sale lots record dividends and check reinvestment across accounts

00:00:30.513 --> 00:00:32.831
The goal is a clear view of what you own

00:00:33.312 --> 00:00:36.424
what your records say and which control to use when

00:00:36.424 --> 00:00:37.505
something needs attention

00:00:39.224 --> 00:00:42.141
Start with the account selector at the top right It

00:00:42.141 --> 00:00:46.255
determines which portfolio you are viewing The Basis selector switches

00:00:46.255 --> 00:00:51.060
between original cost and broker adjusted cost where the application

00:00:51.216 --> 00:00:55.461
has that information Keep the basis consistent when comparing cost

00:00:55.539 --> 00:01:00.084
and gain or loss across pages The toolbar provides Import

00:01:00.097 --> 00:01:05.552
Holdings Transaction History Deposits and Withdrawals the dividend source filter

00:01:05.787 --> 00:01:09.797
price and dividend refresh dividend repair and the two ways

00:01:09.797 --> 00:01:12.883
to add a holding In an aggregate view the page

00:01:12.896 --> 00:01:16.880
identifies how holding edits are routed For a correction to

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:21.099
one specific account select that account first or use the

00:01:21.099 --> 00:01:24.250
expanded transaction ledger’s explicit account selector

00:01:25.954 --> 00:01:31.345
The Post-Refresh Accrual Estimate panel describes income estimated since the

00:01:31.345 --> 00:01:35.134
most recent refresh Each account card shows an account name

00:01:35.472 --> 00:01:39.066
and an accrual amount When payment details are available the

00:01:39.066 --> 00:01:43.389
card lists the ticker expected payment date and amount The

00:01:43.389 --> 00:01:46.371
line below the total may show a count of payments

00:01:46.501 --> 00:01:50.147
since refresh or an estimate over an elapsed number of

00:01:50.147 --> 00:01:54.287
days A dash and no prior refresh mean there is

00:01:54.301 --> 00:01:58.702
no refresh baseline yet Use this panel to identify income

00:01:58.897 --> 00:02:02.569
that may need review It is an accrual view and

00:02:02.569 --> 00:02:06.189
you should compare it with recorded dividend history when confirming

00:02:06.202 --> 00:02:07.907
what actually arrived in the account

00:02:09.634 --> 00:02:12.681
Ticker DRIP Coverage counts the ticker names in the current

00:02:12.681 --> 00:02:16.158
dividend source view The large number is the total count

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:21.236
The green badge shows how many have dividend reinvestment enabled

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:25.142
and the percentage they represent The amber badge shows how

00:02:25.142 --> 00:02:28.853
many do not Every ticker counts once regardless of its

00:02:28.853 --> 00:02:32.915
value share count or dividend rate This makes the box

00:02:32.928 --> 00:02:37.447
useful for checking how widely reinvestment is enabled across the

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:41.457
portfolio A small position has the same weight in this

00:02:41.457 --> 00:02:45.428
count as a large position The count follows the holding’s

00:02:45.441 --> 00:02:49.504
DRIP setting rather than proving that every historical dividend has

00:02:49.517 --> 00:02:51.066
already purchased shares

00:02:52.764 --> 00:02:57.816
The other four boxes describe estimated income Estimated Monthly Income

00:02:58.012 --> 00:03:02.347
is the portfolio’s annual dividend estimate divided by twelve It

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:06.540
is a monthly average so quarterly or uneven payments do

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:11.788
not necessarily arrive in equal monthly amounts Mo dollars Reinvested

00:03:12.113 --> 00:03:16.957
is the estimated monthly income allocated to holdings with reinvestment

00:03:16.970 --> 00:03:22.256
enabled Mo dollars Not Reinvested is the estimated monthly income

00:03:22.413 --> 00:03:28.467
allocated to cash Percent Reinvested divides estimated reinvested income by

00:03:28.571 --> 00:03:33.402
total estimated monthly income These boxes are forward estimates based

00:03:33.402 --> 00:03:37.347
on the recorded dividend inputs and DRIP settings They help

00:03:37.348 --> 00:03:41.071
you see the balance between projected reinvestment and cash income

00:03:41.566 --> 00:03:44.483
they are not a statement of actual cash received this

00:03:44.496 --> 00:03:44.952
month

00:03:46.631 --> 00:03:49.951
Expand Why the DRIP Percentages Can Be Different for an

00:03:49.964 --> 00:03:53.754
explanation built into the screen Suppose two of four tickers

00:03:53.754 --> 00:03:58.311
have DRIP enabled The ticker coverage is fifty percent If

00:03:58.311 --> 00:04:02.243
those two tickers produce twenty dollars of the portfolio’s hundred

00:04:02.243 --> 00:04:06.813
dollars of estimated monthly income the income reinvested percentage is

00:04:06.826 --> 00:04:11.384
only twenty percent Both answers are correct One counts names

00:04:11.644 --> 00:04:16.735
the other counts dollars Share quantities dividend amounts and payment

00:04:16.735 --> 00:04:21.514
frequency affect the dollar calculation In a combined or Owner

00:04:21.514 --> 00:04:24.951
view the same ticker can reinvest in one account and

00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:28.571
take cash in another Review the account-level split when a

00:04:28.571 --> 00:04:31.019
headline percentage needs explanation

00:04:32.737 --> 00:04:35.576
The holdings table has a wide set of fields and

00:04:35.589 --> 00:04:38.310
Columns lets you choose the ones you need Open the

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:41.813
control then search for a field or browse the list

00:04:42.229 --> 00:04:46.084
Each description explains what that column means Uncheck an optional

00:04:46.084 --> 00:04:50.029
column to hide it The ticker stays visible Use the

00:04:50.042 --> 00:04:52.998
up and down buttons drag a row in the menu

00:04:53.505 --> 00:04:56.578
or drag a table header to change the order Show

00:04:56.578 --> 00:05:01.513
all restores all fields Reset order and visibility restores the

00:05:01.526 --> 00:05:05.367
default arrangement On the table click a sortable header to

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:10.524
change the sort direction Horizontal scrolling reveals fields farther across

00:05:10.537 --> 00:05:14.287
the table while header tooltips provide a quick definition

00:05:16.007 --> 00:05:20.890
The Shared Performance Date Range controls the period-dependent performance figures

00:05:21.333 --> 00:05:24.783
One day measures from the previous close seven days looks

00:05:24.796 --> 00:05:29.757
back seven calendar days The month and year presets choose

00:05:29.861 --> 00:05:33.716
calendar-based start dates and year to date starts at January

00:05:33.716 --> 00:05:38.807
first All begins with the portfolio’s own recorded history Custom

00:05:38.807 --> 00:05:44.158
exposes inclusive start and end dates Read the explanatory lines

00:05:44.288 --> 00:05:48.051
for the actual resolved window This control does not hide

00:05:48.064 --> 00:05:52.700
holdings or change the current shares value or cost basis

00:05:53.104 --> 00:05:56.893
The regular gain and loss columns follow the selected window

00:05:57.309 --> 00:06:01.203
Life is different it measures current value against the cost

00:06:01.216 --> 00:06:04.796
of shares still held The separate Life Gain and Loss

00:06:04.809 --> 00:06:07.479
columns retain that cost-basis meaning

00:06:09.174 --> 00:06:12.625
Begin at the left of the table Ticker and Description

00:06:12.742 --> 00:06:17.560
identify the security and Category is the classification assigned to

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:21.062
the holding Percent Account shows its share of current holdings

00:06:21.075 --> 00:06:25.528
value Shares is the current quantity Purchased shows the original

00:06:25.724 --> 00:06:30.385
or earliest lot date Base separates originally purchased shares from

00:06:30.385 --> 00:06:36.010
DRIP Shares acquired through reinvestment Cash Reinvested records the cash

00:06:36.023 --> 00:06:39.669
used for those reinvestments Paid is the average cost per

00:06:39.669 --> 00:06:43.588
share Current is the market price Cost is the position’s

00:06:43.601 --> 00:06:47.494
recorded cost basis and Value is its current market value

00:06:47.911 --> 00:06:53.172
These fields answer different questions quantity purchase history cost and

00:06:53.172 --> 00:06:57.065
today’s valuation Click the ticker to open its research sheet

00:06:57.508 --> 00:06:59.695
or the triangle to inspect its ledger

00:07:01.394 --> 00:07:05.144
Gain and Loss dollars and percent follow the shared range

00:07:05.561 --> 00:07:09.076
Each row describes the ticker’s current lot in that window

00:07:09.493 --> 00:07:14.649
The portfolio total uses the broader tracker price-return calculation which

00:07:14.662 --> 00:07:18.022
can include positions held during the range and fully sold

00:07:18.022 --> 00:07:21.602
afterward That is why a selected-period total should not be

00:07:21.602 --> 00:07:26.967
interpreted as simply adding lifetime open-position gains Life Gain and

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:30.339
Loss is current value minus the cost of the remaining

00:07:30.352 --> 00:07:33.855
shares and its percentage compares that difference with their cost

00:07:34.272 --> 00:07:38.139
Realized Gain and Loss is profit or loss from completed

00:07:38.139 --> 00:07:43.464
sales Keep price performance realized sales and dividends separate when

00:07:43.465 --> 00:07:47.501
explaining results The table’s labels and notes help you compare

00:07:47.501 --> 00:07:49.962
the same scope across the application

00:07:51.641 --> 00:07:56.993
Div dollars is the recent distribution per share Frequency identifies

00:07:57.006 --> 00:08:03.907
the payment cadence weekly monthly quarterly semiannual or annual Ex

00:08:03.907 --> 00:08:08.126
Dividend and Pay Date describe the distribution schedule a pay

00:08:08.126 --> 00:08:12.175
date marked as estimated comes from the projected schedule rather

00:08:12.175 --> 00:08:15.691
than a confirmed payment The DRIP checkbox records whether this

00:08:15.704 --> 00:08:20.287
holding reinvests Changing it updates the application’s setting it does

00:08:20.287 --> 00:08:23.581
not place a broker order Year dollars and Month dollars

00:08:23.581 --> 00:08:28.529
are annual and monthly income estimates DRIP dollars and Cash

00:08:28.542 --> 00:08:33.555
dollars split estimated monthly income according to the reinvestment setting

00:08:33.959 --> 00:08:38.842
Month Shares and Year Shares estimate shares purchasable by reinvesting

00:08:38.972 --> 00:08:43.438
at the current price Those are hypothetical quantities not completed

00:08:43.438 --> 00:08:44.193
purchases

00:08:45.894 --> 00:08:49.709
Yield on Cost compares estimated annual dividends with the recorded

00:08:49.709 --> 00:08:54.175
cost basis Current Yield compares that annual estimate with current

00:08:54.188 --> 00:08:58.251
market value They can differ because your purchase cost differs

00:08:58.251 --> 00:09:01.389
from today’s price The column named for the current month

00:09:01.545 --> 00:09:06.129
shows that month’s holding income figure Dividend Paid Year to

00:09:06.259 --> 00:09:11.519
Date Dividends and Total Dividends summarize the application’s dividend records

00:09:11.936 --> 00:09:15.985
Paid For Itself shows the fraction of original cost recovered

00:09:16.272 --> 00:09:20.842
through cumulative dividends one hundred percent means dividends equal that

00:09:20.842 --> 00:09:25.438
cost Dividend Source identifies where the actuals came from such

00:09:25.438 --> 00:09:30.230
as imported broker history a snapshot or Yahoo If DRIP

00:09:30.464 --> 00:09:34.267
is a hypothetical share calculation at current price rather than

00:09:34.267 --> 00:09:36.910
a record of actual reinvested shares

00:09:38.594 --> 00:09:43.047
Beta describes historical price sensitivity to the benchmark shown for

00:09:43.047 --> 00:09:47.878
that ticker Delta Up and Delta Down estimate sensitivity on

00:09:47.891 --> 00:09:52.435
benchmark up days and down days They are historical relationships

00:09:52.826 --> 00:09:57.956
not guaranteed future moves Return versus Yield compares total return

00:09:57.956 --> 00:10:01.420
with yield on a compatible time basis Its header button

00:10:01.420 --> 00:10:05.951
switches between Yield on Cost and Current Yield Good indicates

00:10:05.951 --> 00:10:10.157
return at least matches the yield comparison Poor indicates the

00:10:10.235 --> 00:10:15.313
income rate exceeds total return Close is the fund closure-risk

00:10:15.313 --> 00:10:19.714
field which concerns a fund issuer closing a small ETF

00:10:20.131 --> 00:10:23.802
Stocks are not rated there Grade is the composite assessment

00:10:23.816 --> 00:10:27.006
for the selected market window and is blank on Life

00:10:27.435 --> 00:10:30.678
Missing data can produce a dash instead of a rating

00:10:32.341 --> 00:10:36.260
At the far right each holding has Edit Transaction and

00:10:36.260 --> 00:10:41.456
Delete controls Edit opens the holding’s basic information dividend settings

00:10:41.729 --> 00:10:47.185
income fields and reinvestment information Transaction opens the purchase and

00:10:47.185 --> 00:10:51.768
sale ledger Use it for trade dates share quantities purchase

00:10:51.846 --> 00:10:56.755
or sale prices and fees Delete is for removing a

00:10:56.755 --> 00:11:01.638
holding from the selected portfolio and presents a confirmation Within

00:11:01.638 --> 00:11:05.909
an expanded ledger Delete acts on one event instead Read

00:11:05.909 --> 00:11:09.411
the confirmation to understand what will be removed As a

00:11:09.411 --> 00:11:14.099
routine workflow open Edit for a category or dividend correction

00:11:14.594 --> 00:11:17.979
and use Transaction when the broker’s trading history needs a

00:11:17.979 --> 00:11:21.534
correction Save only after checking the account and the record

00:11:23.241 --> 00:11:27.890
In the Edit dialog Basic Info contains Ticker Description and

00:11:27.890 --> 00:11:33.215
Category Description and Category make the holding easier to recognize

00:11:33.215 --> 00:11:37.421
and organize Changing the ticker is a rename saving can

00:11:37.421 --> 00:11:43.970
rename it across portfolios transactions dividends categories and ticker settings

00:11:44.400 --> 00:11:48.749
Use that for an actual symbol correction Position contains Shares

00:11:48.970 --> 00:11:53.905
Price Paid Current Price and Purchase Date When transactions exist

00:11:54.153 --> 00:11:58.619
the dialog explains that Shares Price Paid and Purchase Date

00:11:58.684 --> 00:12:03.384
are managed by transactions and disables those fields Correct the

00:12:03.515 --> 00:12:07.408
underlying lots with the Transaction button For a simple holding

00:12:07.525 --> 00:12:12.239
without transaction history those position fields can be entered directly

00:12:12.655 --> 00:12:17.147
Update saves the holding form and Cancel closes it without

00:12:17.160 --> 00:12:17.668
saving

00:12:19.364 --> 00:12:25.093
Dividend Info contains Dividends per Share Frequency DRIP Ex Dividend

00:12:25.093 --> 00:12:28.362
Date and Pay Date Enter the amount for a single

00:12:28.362 --> 00:12:33.752
distribution per share then choose the appropriate cadence Auto allows

00:12:33.752 --> 00:12:38.453
market data detection a manually selected cadence can remain pinned

00:12:38.700 --> 00:12:43.244
until changed The DRIP checkbox tells the application how to

00:12:43.310 --> 00:12:47.541
allocate the holding’s income estimate Enter the schedule dates using

00:12:47.541 --> 00:12:51.096
the format shown in the form Manual amount and date

00:12:51.109 --> 00:12:56.031
corrections can temporarily override automatic data When an override is

00:12:56.044 --> 00:12:59.455
active the form shows its duration and a Use market

00:12:59.468 --> 00:13:03.674
data now link Undo reverses that pending choice Follow the

00:13:03.674 --> 00:13:08.635
displayed note some fields resume market data on save while

00:13:08.648 --> 00:13:10.836
others resume on the next refresh

00:13:12.544 --> 00:13:16.385
Scroll within the holding dialog to Dividend Tracking and Total

00:13:16.385 --> 00:13:21.971
Returns Dividends Paid Year to Date Dividends and Total Dividends

00:13:21.984 --> 00:13:26.268
Received let you maintain the holding’s income totals Check them

00:13:26.268 --> 00:13:30.513
against your actual payment records rather than copying an annual

00:13:30.526 --> 00:13:35.200
estimate into an actual-income field Paid For Itself is stored

00:13:35.213 --> 00:13:38.976
as a ratio a value of one represents one hundred

00:13:38.976 --> 00:13:43.195
percent and the table formats it as a percentage Estimated

00:13:43.208 --> 00:13:48.078
Annual and Monthly Dividend describe projected income On save the

00:13:48.091 --> 00:13:53.234
form recalculates applicable estimates and ratios from the position distribution

00:13:53.456 --> 00:13:59.432
and frequency inputs Reinvestment contains Cash Not Reinvested Cash Reinvested

00:13:59.836 --> 00:14:04.289
and Shares from Dividends Use real history for historical figures

00:14:04.471 --> 00:14:08.182
and review the recalculated values before relying on them

00:14:09.904 --> 00:14:13.732
Add Holding opens the same grouped form with empty fields

00:14:14.149 --> 00:14:18.706
Enter the ticker use Lookup to retrieve available market information

00:14:19.162 --> 00:14:23.133
review the description and category and enter the share quantity

00:14:23.290 --> 00:14:27.925
and purchase details Check the dividend cadence and dates before

00:14:28.068 --> 00:14:33.172
selecting Add Cancel exits without creating the position Add or

00:14:33.290 --> 00:14:36.844
Edit via Transaction is the alternative for starting with a

00:14:36.844 --> 00:14:41.362
trade record Its new-ticker form includes the ticker lookup description

00:14:41.558 --> 00:14:47.079
category trade date shares price per share fees and notes

00:14:47.495 --> 00:14:51.467
A new ticker begins with a buy This establishes transaction

00:14:51.467 --> 00:14:56.623
history that can later drive position calculations Import Holdings provides

00:14:56.623 --> 00:15:00.816
another route when your broker file already contains the positions

00:15:00.933 --> 00:15:01.974
or transactions

00:15:03.684 --> 00:15:07.551
Select the triangle beside a ticker to expand its ledger

00:15:07.968 --> 00:15:12.161
This view brings together trades and actual dividend payments It

00:15:12.161 --> 00:15:17.799
shows event type date shares price fees cost or proceeds

00:15:18.085 --> 00:15:23.137
unrealized gain realized gain and running position average cost and

00:15:23.150 --> 00:15:27.304
total cost Read the event type first a cash dividend

00:15:27.421 --> 00:15:31.327
does not add shares or change the position’s cost basis

00:15:31.744 --> 00:15:36.119
Reinvested shares appear as a separate buy Sortable headers help

00:15:36.132 --> 00:15:39.413
review the entries and the built-in help explains how to

00:15:39.544 --> 00:15:43.202
read and manage the table Edit opens that specific event

00:15:43.346 --> 00:15:47.825
in its actual account Delete removes that event and recalculates

00:15:47.825 --> 00:15:51.301
the holding it is separate from deleting the whole holding

00:15:53.017 --> 00:15:57.392
The Transaction dialog shows saved trades above an Add Transaction

00:15:57.392 --> 00:16:01.533
form Choose Buy to record purchased shares enter the actual

00:16:01.533 --> 00:16:06.090
trade date share quantity price per share and any fees

00:16:06.390 --> 00:16:09.827
then add a note if useful Originally Acquired is for

00:16:09.827 --> 00:16:14.567
shares transferred from another broker it preserves the original acquisition

00:16:14.567 --> 00:16:18.707
date separately from the transfer-related record Leave it blank for

00:16:18.707 --> 00:16:22.666
an ordinary purchase To correct a saved trade select its

00:16:22.796 --> 00:16:26.233
Edit control The form loads that event and its save

00:16:26.246 --> 00:16:30.921
control updates the existing transaction Cancel Edit returns to adding

00:16:30.934 --> 00:16:35.673
a new event Close exits the dialog Recording or correcting

00:16:35.673 --> 00:16:40.999
trades recalculates the position and cost basis so verify quantities

00:16:40.999 --> 00:16:42.861
and prices against the source record

00:16:44.554 --> 00:16:48.005
Choose Sell to record a completed sale The form changes

00:16:48.005 --> 00:16:51.924
to Shares Sold and displays available shares when open lots

00:16:51.924 --> 00:16:57.302
are present Enter the sale date quantity execution price fees

00:16:57.549 --> 00:17:02.223
and notes FIFO is the default cost-basis method it matches

00:17:02.223 --> 00:17:07.106
the oldest available purchase lots first Specific Lots displays the

00:17:07.171 --> 00:17:12.302
eligible buy dates prices cost per share and available quantities

00:17:12.705 --> 00:17:16.820
Enter the quantity sold from each lot those allocations are

00:17:16.820 --> 00:17:20.427
summed into the sale quantity Match this to the lot

00:17:20.427 --> 00:17:25.179
treatment documented in your broker records The application then recalculates

00:17:25.179 --> 00:17:29.802
the remaining shares cost basis and realized gain or loss

00:17:30.231 --> 00:17:34.710
These controls record transactions in Portfolio Tracker they do not

00:17:34.723 --> 00:17:36.390
execute a trade at your broker

00:17:38.094 --> 00:17:40.295
When more than one buy or sell occurs for the

00:17:40.295 --> 00:17:44.722
same ticker account and date the Same Day Order controls

00:17:44.735 --> 00:17:48.081
show up and down arrows Use them to match the

00:17:48.094 --> 00:17:51.675
broker’s actual execution order They do not move a trade

00:17:51.675 --> 00:17:55.672
onto a different date or into another account FIFO matching

00:17:55.750 --> 00:18:00.073
and cost basis recalculate after each move Only Trade means

00:18:00.073 --> 00:18:04.292
there is no other qualifying trade to reorder Not Applicable

00:18:04.292 --> 00:18:08.289
marks a dividend payment because cash dividends do not affect

00:18:08.302 --> 00:18:12.261
FIFO trade order In the expanded ledger use Edit when

00:18:12.274 --> 00:18:16.441
the event belongs on another date If the application identifies

00:18:16.454 --> 00:18:21.050
missing opening history or an unpriced purchase repair that source

00:18:21.050 --> 00:18:24.800
record before assuming a sale’s unavailable gain is zero

00:18:26.474 --> 00:18:30.836
The expanded ledger’s Add Transaction control asks for an account

00:18:31.149 --> 00:18:34.508
and a transaction type Choose Buy or Sell for a

00:18:34.521 --> 00:18:38.557
trade or Dividend Payment for an actual cash payment then

00:18:38.558 --> 00:18:43.258
Continue The dividend form shows the account payment date cash

00:18:43.258 --> 00:18:46.722
amount and notes Enter the total cash payment for the

00:18:46.722 --> 00:18:51.214
event rather than a per-share dividend estimate then use Save

00:18:51.227 --> 00:18:56.357
Dividend Cancel leaves the record unchanged An existing dividend event

00:18:56.370 --> 00:19:01.044
has its own Edit control A reinvested dividend needs its

00:19:01.045 --> 00:19:04.990
cash payment recorded here and the resulting shares recorded as

00:19:05.003 --> 00:19:09.365
a separate buy transaction Keeping both events distinct preserves a

00:19:09.365 --> 00:19:12.789
clear view of income received and the shares acquired with

00:19:12.789 --> 00:19:13.427
that income

00:19:15.144 --> 00:19:20.392
Transaction History opens the account’s saved buys sells and actual

00:19:20.405 --> 00:19:24.337
dividends including tickers that are no longer held Search by

00:19:24.350 --> 00:19:29.233
ticker account or notes filter by event type and select

00:19:29.233 --> 00:19:34.389
Closed Positions Only when reviewing past positions Deposits and Withdrawals

00:19:34.558 --> 00:19:38.816
serves a different purpose It records money added or removed

00:19:39.090 --> 00:19:43.399
and share transfers so Account Alpha can separate external funding

00:19:43.399 --> 00:19:46.811
from investment performance Add a missing event with its type

00:19:47.110 --> 00:19:52.397
date amount or share details and note The completed-period controls

00:19:52.501 --> 00:19:57.201
identify stretches with a complete cash-flow record including periods where

00:19:57.201 --> 00:20:01.160
no money moved Mark a period complete only after all

00:20:01.160 --> 00:20:05.353
its flows are present That completeness determines when Account Alpha

00:20:05.548 --> 00:20:06.303
can be measured

00:20:08.014 --> 00:20:11.933
All Dividend Sources filters the table and summary counts by

00:20:11.933 --> 00:20:16.426
the source of dividend actuals Selecting a source changes the

00:20:16.439 --> 00:20:20.866
view it does not repair the underlying record Refresh Prices

00:20:21.009 --> 00:20:26.361
and Dividends updates market inputs After a refresh Latest Refresh

00:20:26.374 --> 00:20:31.374
Result can show payable distributions changed holding dividend fields and

00:20:31.374 --> 00:20:36.608
payment-history rows recorded updated or already present The Dividend Repair

00:20:36.608 --> 00:20:42.051
mode chooses imported actuals plus Yahoo imported actuals only or

00:20:42.064 --> 00:20:46.894
Yahoo only Preview Dividend Repair shows the proposed repair scope

00:20:47.168 --> 00:20:51.556
source counts and any date or amount updates Inspect those

00:20:51.569 --> 00:20:56.634
details before selecting Apply Repair Cancel leaves the repair unapplied

00:20:57.051 --> 00:21:01.022
Preview and refresh may take time wait for the completed

00:21:01.022 --> 00:21:03.053
result before reviewing the figures

00:21:04.774 --> 00:21:07.951
The Owner view adds DRIP Matrix and Sync DRIP from

00:21:07.951 --> 00:21:12.821
Accounts The matrix puts ticker rows against account columns so

00:21:12.834 --> 00:21:16.167
you can inspect whether the same security reinvests in each

00:21:16.167 --> 00:21:21.128
account Use Filter Ticker to find one symbol Each checkbox

00:21:21.141 --> 00:21:24.865
belongs to that ticker in a specific account and toggling

00:21:24.865 --> 00:21:29.371
it updates that account’s application record Sync to Owner consolidates

00:21:29.436 --> 00:21:33.446
the account-level DRIP flags and share counts into the Owner

00:21:33.459 --> 00:21:38.186
view The toolbar’s Sync DRIP from Accounts performs that synchronization

00:21:38.199 --> 00:21:42.834
directly Review the account settings before syncing particularly where the

00:21:42.834 --> 00:21:46.493
same ticker takes cash in one account and reinvests in

00:21:46.506 --> 00:21:51.141
another These settings track your reinvestment choices in the application

00:21:51.584 --> 00:21:53.693
brokerage instructions remain separate

00:21:55.394 --> 00:21:59.261
A practical routine begins with the correct account and basis

00:21:59.652 --> 00:22:03.858
Review the income and DRIP boxes choose a performance window

00:22:04.261 --> 00:22:06.592
and arrange the table around the fields you want to

00:22:06.605 --> 00:22:11.332
compare Open Edit for holding information and dividend settings Open

00:22:11.332 --> 00:22:16.267
the transaction ledger for purchases sales and actual dividend events

00:22:16.670 --> 00:22:21.175
Compare history with your broker records review repair previews and

00:22:21.188 --> 00:22:25.264
use the cross-account matrix when managing the Owner view Portfolio

00:22:25.277 --> 00:22:29.209
Tracker brings those details together so you can maintain clearer

00:22:29.209 --> 00:22:34.183
records and understand what each number represents For informational purposes

